{
  "version": "budget-pixel-v2",
  "forBand": "docs/band-pixel-v2.json",
  "bandVersion": "pixel-v2",
  "method": "Leave-one-out across the band's own crops. For each crop i the p05/p95 band is rebuilt from the other N-1 crops (identical widening rule, via metrics.mjs bandIntervals) and crop i is scored against it. The budget is p95 of the resulting fail-count distribution, rounded up. Mirrors the audio side (docs/BAR.md): an all-pass gate rejects genuine work.",
  "sampling": {
    "crops": 128,
    "size": 320,
    "seed": "fixel-band-v1",
    "inset": 24,
    "rng": "src/core/rng.js Rng(seed).stream(\"crops\")"
  },
  "source": "refs/EBY-LA-Hot-Dog-175k.png",
  "gate": "hardFail",
  "gateComment": "Score with tools/metrics.mjs --band <band> --budget <file.png>. ACCEPT when the number of HARD failures (out of band on the side the band file calls a real craft defect) is <= budget.hardFail. Advisory-side out-of-band readings are not defects and are not counted, exactly as in printScore. The gate reads the median-of-crops composite, which is what metrics.mjs --band already scores.",
  "budget": {
    "hardFail": 31,
    "anyFail": 22,
    "clusterFail": 15
  },
  "budgetDerivation": {
    "looP95": 19.299999999999983,
    "looBudget": 20,
    "widenedToAcceptGenuineWork": 11,
    "widenComment": "The leave-one-out p95 over crops of a single artwork is 20. That budget rejects genuine work in the same craft family (refs/C3L Lufthansa Frankfurt Pixorama 45k.png = 27), because crop-to-crop variation within one artwork is a strict subset of artwork-to-artwork variation and the LOO corpus contains exactly one artwork. Widened to the smallest integer that accepts every --accept file, and no further.",
    "rejectMargin": 17,
    "separatesAcceptFromReject": true
  },
  "validity": {
    "usableAsFloorGate": true,
    "usableAsScore": false,
    "inversions": [
      {
        "generator": "out/look/r2check.png",
        "beats": "refs/C3L Lufthansa Frankfurt Pixorama 45k.png",
        "by": 8
      }
    ],
    "comment": "RANKING INVERTED: a --generator file scores FEWER hard fails than genuine work in the same craft family. The count therefore measures proximity to this band's centre, not craft. Use the budget only to reject things outside the family; use the HARD-FAIL LIST, never the count, to say how good something is. This is BAR.md's \"weight the hard-fail list; never the pass count\" showing up as a measurement rather than as advice."
  },
